  "Id": 1021,
  "Title": "AKU reflects Islamic way of life - says CPLC chief Jameel Yusuf",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "In keeping with its tradition, Aga Khan University (AKU) celebrated Independence Day on August 14, 2001.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassF700C7F61D5A483DA44E58A2BC43EFD4\"><div>\u200bIn keeping with its tradition, Aga Khan University (AKU) celebrated Independence Day on August 14, 2001. The chief guest, Mr. Jameel Yusuf, Chief, Citizen-Police Liaison Committee (CPLC), urged citizens to work in areas of health, education and law and order, and lauded AKU for being an institution &quot;that reflects the Islamic way of existence.&quot; Felicitating the jubilant guests on the nation's 54th birth anniversary, Dr. Shamsh Kassim-Lakha, President, AKU, suggested focus on human resources and underlined the importance of research in dealing with problems facing society.</div></div>",
